Abort the export when the archive does not open

The export tested the result of the archive open without a negation. A
successful open therefore ended the export at once, the dialog reported
a failure, and an empty archive stayed on disk.

Negate the test. The export now goes on after a successful open, and it
stops only when the open fails.

The change sits on the branch work/presets of the local tree, as commit 2 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index bd6344c2..6b746070 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -2901,7 +2901,7 @@ void QtCurveConfig::exportPreset()
     if (!file.isEmpty()) {
         bool rv = [&] {
             std::unique_ptr<KZip> zip(compressed ? new KZip(file) : nullptr);
-            if (zip && zip->open(QIODevice::WriteOnly))
+            if (zip && !zip->open(QIODevice::WriteOnly))
                 return false;
             std::unique_ptr<QTemporaryFile> temp(
                 compressed ? new QTemporaryFile() : nullptr);
